<title>GERMANY: First Deutsche Bank board female dies.</title>
<headline>First Deutsche Bank board female dies.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ellen Schneider-Lenne, a well-known management board member at Deutsche Bank AG, died on Christmas Day aged 54, the German bank said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>Schneider-Lenne, the first woman to ever sit on Deutsche board, had asked to step down from the board prior to her death which the bank only said was because of a serious illness.</p>
